IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. DB2VSAM1.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
   SELECT VSAMFILE ASSIGN TO VSAMDD
         ORGANIZTION IS INDEXED
         ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
         RECORD KEY IS VSAM-ACC-NO
         FILE STATUS IS WS-FILE-STATUS.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD VSAMFILE
   RECORD CONTAINS 71 CHARACTERS
   01 VSAM-RECORD.
      05 VSAM-ACC-NO PIC X(10).
      05 VSAM-CUST-NAME   PIC X(30).
      05 VSAM-BALANCE PIC 9(9)V99 COMP-3.
      05 VSAM-TRANS-AMT PIC 9(9)V99 COMP-3.
      05 VSAM-AVAILABLE-BAL PIC 9(9)V99 COMP-3.
      05 VSAM-STATUS PIC X(1).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
** HOST VARIABLES  **
EXEC SQL
    INCLUDE SQLCA
END-EXEC.

EXEC SQL
    INCLUDE BANK
END-EXEC.

01 WS-ACC-NO PIC X(10).
01 WS-CUST-NAME PIC X(30).
01 WS-BALANCE PIC 9(9)V99 COMP-3.
01 WS-TRANS-AMT PIC 9(9)V99 COMP-3.
01 WS-AVAILABLE-BAL PIC 9(9)V99 COMP-3.
01 WS-STATUS PIC X(1).

**  FILE STATUS **
01 WS-FILE-STATUS PIC XX.
   88 WS-FILE-OK VALUE '00'.
   88 WS-FILE-NOT-FOUND VALUE '23'.
   88 WS-FILE-ALREADY-EXISTS VALUE '22'.
   88 WS-FILE-ERROR VALUE '99'.

** COUNTERS **
01 WS-READ-COUNT PIC 9(5) VALUE 0.
01 WS-WRITE-COUNT PIC 9(5) VALUE 0.
01 WS-ERROR-COUNT PIC 9(5) VALUE 0.

** CONSTANTS **
01 WS-EOF PIC X VALUE 'N'.
   88 WS-END-OF-DATA VALUE 'Y'.

01 WS-VALID-RECORD PIC X VALUE 'Y'.
   88 WS-RECORD-VALID VALUE 'Y'.
   88 WS-RECORD-INVALID VALUE 'N'.